# Beamline Assistant - Server Configuration
#
# Define which analysis servers to load
# Format: server_name:path/to/server.py
#
# To enable/disable a server, comment/uncomment the line
# To add a new server, add a new line with the same format

# Core Beamline Operations (UNIFIED SERVER - Replaces 3 servers)
# Combines: filesystem, command executor, X-ray utilities
# Provides: file ops, safe command execution, X-ray calculations
# 🎯 Optimized for ARGO AI: Fewer tools, better performance
core:beamline_core_server.py

# MIDAS analysis adapters
# Provides FF/NF/PF-HEDM, detector calibration/integration and materials analysis.
# Some tools call MIDAS executables; others are APEXA adapters or need optional packages.
midas:midas_comprehensive_server.py

# EPICS Motor Control (Channel Access via caget/caput)
# Provides motor position read, absolute/relative move, jog, tweak, homing
# Requires EPICS base tools (caget/caput) on PATH and IOC running
motor:epics_motor_server.py

# Beamline Alignment (apexa_alignment_server)
# General-purpose alignment helper: VOCS-based task library (rotation axis,
# SAXS beam-on-beamstop centering, slit tuning to historical IC targets,
# diode-max 1D scans), SQLite history DB, PVA stream analysis.
# Base install works offline (analytical fits + history ingest/query).
# Live motion + Bayesian optimization needs the [alignment] extra:
#   uv sync --extra alignment   (installs xopt + pvapy)
# AlignmentAgent routes on "align", "beamstop", "hotspot", "rotation axis",
# "tune slits", "pva stream", etc.  Operating card lives in
# knowledge_base/capsules/beamline-alignment/.
alignment:apexa_alignment_server.py

# ===== LEGACY SERVERS (REPLACED BY UNIFIED CORE SERVER) =====
# The following servers are now consolidated into beamline_core_server.py
# Uncomment only if you need them separately for debugging
# filesystem:filesystem_server.py
# executor:command_executor_server.py
# utilities:analysis_utilities_server.py

# GSAS-II - Agentic Rietveld refinement (Agentic-GSAS-II)
# Autonomous parameter selection, COD structure retrieval, trust verdict.
# For MIDAS caked .zarr.zip output use midas:run_gsas_refinement instead.
# Needs the GSAS-II conda env; set APEXA_GSASII_PYTHON / APEXA_AGENTIC_GSAS2
# if they are not at their defaults.
gsas2:gsas2_server.py

# Tomography - TomoPy (APS-standard) parallel-beam tomography for 1-ID / 20-ID
# survey_tomo_stack (pre-flight) + run_tomo_reconstruction (normalize → center →
# recon → optional mask), driven by the `tomo` capsule's hard rules.
# Routes to a native tomo conda env; set APEXA_TOMO_PYTHON to an env that has
# tomopy + dxchange. With no such env the tools return a structured error.
tomo:tomo_server.py

# In-situ synthesis XRD - batch phase evolution vs temperature (I. A. Shkrob's methods)
# synth_inspect_series / synth_pca_map / synth_fit_series / synth_recommend_step /
# synth_fit_kinetics / synth_report. Advisory only: nothing is actuated.
# Routes to its own Python 3.12 env (APEXA_SYNTH_PYTHON: gemmi, lmfit, numpy>=2, h5py,
# pandas, tables, deap). synth_fit_series also needs APEXA_SYNTH_CODE -> the directory
# holding the collaborator's XRD_gemmi.py (unreleased; not shipped with APEXA).
# Missing env -> structured error. Setup: docs/SYNTHESIS_SETUP.md.
synthesis:synthesis_server.py

# MAUD is an optional backend for MIDAS `run_gsas_refinement(engine="maud")`.
# That adapter supports MIDAS caked archives and requires MAUD, MILK and a JDK.
# This standalone server is not included/configured here.
# maud:maud_server.py

# Optional PyFAI server: disabled; no APEXA pyFAI executor is currently registered.
# pyfai:pyfai_server.py

# DIOPTAS - Data Integration and Observation Platform
# Provides interactive data processing, calibration
# dioptas:dioptas_server.py

# Custom Analysis Tools
# Add your own servers here
# custom:custom_analysis_server.py
